{
  "protocol_md": "## Protocol\n\nPrecommitted before this sample was scored:\n\n- Score: trailing excess Sharpe versus T-bills, looked up on the first session of each year from 2011, using only returns strictly before that session. A book needs 756 sessions. Ties break alphabetically. The fallback is the equal-risk long book.\n- The primary set is the equal-risk risk-budget book (long-only and long/short), HRP and mean-variance long-only, the same long-only and long/short books with alphas gated on trailing Sharpe, ridge and gradient boosting (long-only and long/short), the long-only book with a two-state HMM instead of the volatility/trend rule, ridge with meta-label sizing, and the long-only book plus a BTC trend satellite capped at 15%. Leave-one-out alphas, the stock sleeve, and the cost-stress rerun are counted or disclosed and are not in the selector.\n- Machine learning is one of those books. It is used when the selector's past window prefers it. A separate horse race asks whether the fixed ridge or gradient-boosting path beats fixed equal-risk by 0.05 Sharpe on the out-of-sample window. That horse race does not override the selector.\n- A component \"added value\" when the fixed equal-risk long Sharpe on the out-of-sample window exceeds the leave-one-out Sharpe by at least 0.02. That table is a diagnostic. It does not pick a new book after the fact.\n- Endorsement requires all of: out-of-sample CAGR above SPY and above the final SPY/UPRO trend-core on the same sessions, deflated Sharpe at least 0.95 on the persistent ledger, 5-year block-bootstrap probability at least 0.55 of beating each of those two benchmarks (20,000 paths, 63-day blocks, seed 7, $5,000), and a realized max drawdown no worse than 40% for the primary path or 35% for the long-only path. If both paths qualify, the higher CAGR is the recommendation. If neither qualifies, the bot file is 100% SPY and is not endorsed.\n- Costs: 5 bps one-way, plus square-root impact at a $5,000 account, plus 50 bps a year of borrow on short notional and 40 bps of financing above T-bills when the book borrows cash. Rebalance is monthly. The signal is fixed at the close and filled at the next open.\n- The stock sleeve is a fixed list of companies that are still listed. It is ineligible for the recommendation.",
  "caveats": [
    "Single-name momentum uses today's survivors. Delisted companies are missing, so that sleeve is biased upward and cannot be the recommendation.",
    "BTC is the crypto asset that became the liquid major. The satellite is a form of selection. It is eligible only as a capped overlay, and the caveat stays attached to the result.",
    "Equity carry is a five-year reversal, not a dividend yield. The adjusted-price cache does not keep a point-in-time dividend. Commodity carry is absent because the free daily bars do not include a futures curve.",
    "The HMM and the gradient-boosting model are fit only on data available at each refit. A missing alpha is a neutral score, not a zero-imputed fundamental.",
    "Drawdown throttling scales the finished daily path. It is causal, and it is not a second pass of the fill simulator.",
    "Square-root impact uses a coefficient of 0.5. That is a model, not a fit to our fills. On liquid ETFs a $5,000 account pays almost nothing. The $10 million rerun is the capacity check.",
    "Hierarchical risk parity and mean-variance are projected onto the position limits by clipping. They are not the output of a commercial quadratic solver.",
    "This is research on public prices. It is not a recommendation to use leverage, shorts, or leveraged ETFs."
  ],
